        en: 'Across three lessons you borrowed symbols from the book: \\S, [0-9.] and + — today the full dictionary opens: classes describing any character group you pick, ready-made shorthands for the famous ones, and repeaters stretching from zero to a count you set. With these pieces a pattern becomes a miniature program. By the end of this lesson you will be able to: write ranged classes like [a-z0-9], wield \\d and \\w and \\s and \\S and the wildcard dot, choose * or + or ? or {n,m} to fit the question, and tame greedy matching with lazy.',
