        en: "\\d+ caught ['12', '3'] — digits only; \\w+ caught ['room', '12', 'floor', '3'] — letters, digits and underscores. The comma belongs to neither class, so it acts like a fence cutting the harvest, the way split cut words at blanks in chapter 8. The class defines which characters qualify; the repeater defines how many you need.",
      },
    },
    {
      kind: 'concept',
